Module tailrace "The Calf in the Tail-Race" {
  Kind tr_herring "a string of herring" is gear worth 1 weighing 1 described "Six herring on a withy, stiff and bright, smelling of the sea they have just left.".
  Kind tr_mallet "Agnel Thord's drawing-mallet" is gear worth 2 weighing 3 described "A beech mallet the size of a child, its face dished by thirty-one years of knocking stop-logs home.".
  Kind tr_horn "Maric Selle's horn" is gear worth 4 weighing 1 described "A ram's horn, bound in tarred cord, with a mouthpiece worn to the shape of one man's lip.".
  Kind tr_splinter "a splinter of tarred oak" is treasure worth 0 weighing 0 described "A finger of black oak as long as a candle, with a brass nail still through it. It came out of a living thing, and it is warm.".

  Measure fed(entity). Measure wetCount(entity). Measure feedBar(group).
  Relation mabetAsked(group). Relation mabetTrusts(group). Relation splinterDrawn(group). Relation splinterShown(group).
  Relation pressPledged(group). Relation stayed(group). Relation knivesHidden(group). Relation waricWary(group).
  Relation ulkinWarned(group). Relation hayMoved(group). Relation mallet_lent(group). Relation sillForced(group).
  Relation maricYields(group). Relation maricCalls(group). Relation hornSounded(group). Relation damAnswered(group).
  Relation harpooned(group). Relation lightSeen(group). Relation fateTold(entity).

  Discovery law_known "A great fish in the Rì's water is the Rì's, to be boiled for the lamps of the Star-Readers' towers. The gauger's boilers begin on the dawn of the third day.".
  Discovery lampboy_known "Waric Holle trimmed wicks in a Star-Reader's tower for nine years. The lamps have cost more since the whalers stopped coming.".
  Discovery press_known "The mill's rape-press stands idle while the wheel is stopped. Turning, it gives forty gallons of lamp-oil a week.".
  Discovery feed_known "The calf wants three good feeds, of herring or of cold water by the bucket, before the spring tide, or it will not be strong enough to swim.".
  Discovery scar_known "The calf's left flank is scarred by a cord, and a splinter of tarred oak with a brass nail through it is still in the scar.".
  Discovery sill_known "The pond's sill is held by stop-logs. Drawn at the top of the spring tide, the sea comes over and floats the race; drawn earlier, it only drowns Ulkin's meadow.".
  Discovery dam_known "An old whale has lain off the bar for eleven nights, calling. Tolt calls her the Dam.".
  Discovery horn_known "Maric Selle's horn answers the Dam, and the Dam answers it.".
  Discovery plan_known "Maric means to take the Dam when she comes in for her calf: sixty barrels, with a harpoon of his own forging.".
  Discovery intent_known "The Good Intent, Maric Selle's boat, went up on the Dam's back last March with his brother Joss in her, when she was between the boat and her calf.".
  Discovery cold_known "On a dark tide the loch burns where it is stirred.".

  // ── The calf ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Thing calf "the calf" at tailrace {
    State wedged "A whale calf lies wedged nose-up in the tail-race, grey and glossy, with an eye the colour of a plum. It breathes in long wet sighs.".
    State afloat "The race is brimming. The calf has come up off the stone and hangs in the water with its tail moving, listening.".
    State gone "The tail-race is full of nothing but water, and the wheel has begun, slowly, to turn.".
    State dead "The calf lies still in the race. Its eye has gone dull.".
    State butchered "The race runs red and thick under the wheel, and the boilers' fire is lit on the bank.".
  }
  Observe calf_hungry at tailrace as sign when state(calf, wedged) and fed(calf) == 0 "The calf noses at the empty water. Its flank has begun to show the line of its ribs.".
  Observe calf_fed at tailrace as sign when state(calf, wedged) and fed(calf) >= 3 "The calf is brighter-eyed than it was. It follows your hands.".
  Observe scar_seen near calf when tried(calf, looking) and state(calf, wedged) "On the calf's left flank a cord has bitten deep into the skin and healed over it. In the scar, driven in like a nail in a post, is a finger of black oak with a brass nail through it." teaches scar_known.

  Action feed_calf(actor: group, site: place) "Throw the calf a string of herring" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(calf, site) and state(calf, wedged) and holding(actor, tr_herring).
    Time 2.
    On success { Spend tr_herring from actor. Increase fed(calf) by 1. }
    Result "The calf takes the herring one at a time, as if it were being polite, and the water comes up through its blowhole in a small grateful fountain.".
  }
  Action wet_calf(actor: group, site: place) "Wet the calf down with a bucket-chain" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(calf, site) and state(calf, wedged) and wetCount(calf) * 72 <= watch(clock).
    Time 6.
    On success { Increase wetCount(calf) by 1. Increase fed(calf) by 1. }
    Result "For an hour you carry water up from the pond in a bucket and pour it down the calf's back, and it shivers all the way along, like a horse. By the end the sacking on its flank is steaming and it has stopped sighing.".
  }
  Action draw_splinter(actor: group, site: place) "Draw the splinter out of the calf's flank" {
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(calf, site) and state(calf, wedged) and knows(actor, scar_known) and mabetTrusts(actor) and not splinterDrawn(actor).
    Time 2.
    On success { Assert splinterDrawn(actor). Give tr_splinter to actor. }
    Result "Mabet takes the calf's head in both arms and tells it about leeks. You get your fingers round the oak and pull, and it comes slowly, with a sound like a boot out of mud. The calf lows once, a note you feel in your teeth, and then lies still, and its eye rolls round to look at you.".
  }

  // ── The sill and the meadow ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Thing sill_logs "the stop-logs" at sill {
    State shut "The stop-logs stand in their grooves, pinned.".
    State drawn "The stop-logs are out and the sea is pouring through the sill, black and fast, into the pond.".
    Change draw "Draw the stop-logs with Agnel's mallet" from shut to drawn needing tr_mallet when tideOn() "The tide is a hand's breadth too low to lift the race. Draw the logs now and the pond drains for nothing.".
    Change force "Break the stop-logs out with a crowbar" from shut to drawn needing crowbar when tideOn() "Nor will a crowbar help before the tide.".
  }
  Rule force_marks when state(sill_logs, drawn) and not holding(party, tr_mallet) and not sillForced(party) { Assert sillForced(party). }

  // ── The loch's cold light, which is there whether or not anyone is saved ──────────────────────────────────────────
  Thing coldlight "the loch off the hard" at hard {
    State dark "The loch off the hard lies flat and grey, with a skin of weed along the shingle.".
    State stirred "Where you have stirred it the water burns pale green, in coils, and goes on burning after your hand is out.".
    Change stir "Trail a hand through the loch" from dark to stirred when dark() "In daylight it is only water.".
    Wonder natural rare for aesthetic "Where a ripple turns, the water has a faint green cast, as if something under it were thinking of light. The loch is lit from within, and wants only the dark and a hand to say so.".
  }
}
